{"name":"Make-Up Blue","hex":"#335f8d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"make","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To create.\nTo build, construct, produce, or originate.","To build, construct, produce, or originate."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Brand; marque; manufacturer; maker.","Manner or style of construction (style of how a thing is made)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/make"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cosmetics","blocks":[{"text":"Cosmetics are substances that are intended for application to the body for cleansing, beautifying, promoting attractiveness, or altering appearance. They are mixtures of chemical compounds derived from either natural sources or created synthetically. The products serve various purposes, including personal and skin care. They can also be used to conceal blemishes and enhance natural features. Makeup can add color to the face, enhance features, or alter appearance to resemble a different person, creature, or object."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Cosmetics.JPG/330px-Cosmetics.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cosmetics","wikidata":"Q131207"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Self_make_up_by_an_artist.jpg/500px-Self_make_up_by_an_artist.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Self_make_up_by_an_artist.jpg/1280px-Self_make_up_by_an_artist.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Self_make_up_by_an_artist.jpg/500px-Self_make_up_by_an_artist.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An actor applying bold makeup for a stage performance","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASelf_make_up_by_an_artist.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Marcus_Stewart_and_Mariana_Catalina_in_Oresteia_by_Aeschylus%2C_adapted_by_Ryan_Castalia_for_Stairwell_Theater2%2C_2019.jpg/500px-Marcus_Stewart_and_Mariana_Catalina_in_Oresteia_by_Aeschylus%2C_adapted_by_Ryan_Castalia_for_Stairwell_Theater2%2C_2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Marcus_Stewart_and_Mariana_Catalina_in_Oresteia_by_Aeschylus%2C_adapted_by_Ryan_Castalia_for_Stairwell_Theater2%2C_2019.jpg/1280px-Marcus_Stewart_and_Mariana_Cat